{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","id":"msg_01QkyPc21sXrdR4H2k918Myo","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## Step 1: Analysis of Project Context\n\nThe project context provides VISION.yaml, ARCHITECTURE.yaml, and roadmap/analysis inline. All required information is available without reading files.\n\n## Step 2: Project State Summary\n\n**Problem**: Classic Unix utilities have no formal specs. Man pages omit edge cases, flag interactions, and exit-code contracts. This project derives formal specs from C source, generates Go implementations via AI, and verifies parity via differential testing.\n\n**Architecture**:\n- `docs/` — Human-authored PRDs, use cases, test suites (pipeline reads, never writes)\n- `pkg/sys/` — Darwin/Linux syscall abstractions (golang.org/x/sys wrapper)\n- `pkg/format/` — Column alignment, ANSI colors, human-readable size formatting\n- `pkg/testutils/` — Differential testing harness (run Go binary + GNU reference, compare outputs)\n- `cmd/<utility>/` — Go implementation per utility + differential tests\n- `magefiles/` — Mage build targets (cobbler-scaffold provided; only `cmd/version` is a generation target)\n\n**Current state**: Working branch has specs only. Generated code (pkg/testutils, pkg/sys, pkg/format, cmd/ts, cmd/cat, cmd/wc, cmd/sponge) lives at `generation-merged` tags. All use cases on the working branch show `codestatus: not started`.\n\n**Active release**: `rel00.0` — Batch 0, foundational infrastructure. Use cases:\n- `uc001-magefiles` → `cmd/version` — spec_complete, not started\n- `uc002-format` → `pkg/format` — specstatus: implemented, codestatus: not started\n- `uc003-sys` → `pkg/sys` — spec_complete, not started\n- `uc004-testutils` → `pkg/testutils` — specstatus: implemented, not started\n\n## Step 3: Priority Reasoning\n\nPer P8 (canonical ordering): libraries before consumers; within same tier, alphabetical by path.\n\n- `pkg/format` (f) has no internal dependencies — can be implemented immediately\n- `pkg/sys` (s) has no internal dependencies — alphabetically after format\n- `pkg/testutils` (t) may consume pkg/sys — must follow\n- `cmd/version` (cmd/) is a consumer — must follow all pkg/ work\n\n**First task**: `pkg/format` — column alignment, ANSI color codes, and human-readable size formatting (uc002-format). No dependencies on other pkg/ components.\n\nPer P2: split implementation and tests into separate tasks. With 1-task limit, propose implementation only (no test file).\n\n## Step 4 & 5: Proposed Tasks\n\n```yaml\n- index: 0\n  title: \"pkg/format R1-R3 -- column alignment, ANSI color, and size formatting (uc002-format)\"\n  dependency: -1\n  description: |\n    deliverable_type: code\n\n    required_reading:\n      - docs/ARCHITECTURE.yaml (pkg/format component capabilities, DD3 shared library pattern, technology choices)\n      - docs/specs/use-cases/rel00.0-uc002-format.yaml (pkg/format use case for rel00.0)\n      - docs/specs/product-requirements/ (locate and read prdNNN-format.yaml -- the PRD for pkg/format; list the directory to find the exact filename)\n\n    files:\n      - path: pkg/format/column.go\n        action: create\n        note: \"Column alignment types and functions for tabular output -- derive exact exported type names from PRD\"\n      - path: pkg/format/color.go\n        action: create\n        note: \"ANSI color escape code constants and helper functions -- derive exact exported names from PRD\"\n      - path: pkg/format/size.go\n        action: create\n        note: \"Human-readable byte-count formatting functions -- derive exact exported names from PRD\"\n\n    requirements:\n      - id: R1\n        text: \"Implement column alignment for tabular output per pkg/format PRD R1 -- provide functions or types to align multi-column output with configurable per-column widths, supporting ls -l style listings\"\n      - id: R2\n        text: \"Implement ANSI color code output per pkg/format PRD R2 -- provide constants or functions returning ANSI escape sequences for file types (regular file, directory, symbolic link, executable) and permission bit display\"\n      - id: R3\n        text: \"Implement human-readable size formatting per pkg/format PRD R3 -- convert byte counts to K/M/G suffixed strings matching GNU coreutils --human-readable output format\"\n      - id: R4\n        text: \"pkg/format must depend only on the Go standard library -- must not import golang.org/x/sys, any other external package, pkg/sys, or cmd/ packages\"\n\n    design_decisions:\n      - id: D1\n        text: \"Shared library pattern per ARCHITECTURE.yaml DD3 -- common output formatting logic lives in pkg/format and is imported by cmd/ packages; no formatting logic is duplicated across cmd/ packages\"\n      - id: D2\n        text: \"No external dependencies -- pkg/format uses only the Go standard library; golang.org/x/sys is reserved for pkg/sys only per ARCHITECTURE.yaml technology choices\"\n      - id: D3\n        text: \"File names must be derived from primary exported types named in the PRD, not from the package name -- pkg/format/format.go is forbidden by the project naming convention; use type-named files unless the PRD specifies different names\"\n\n    acceptance_criteria:\n      - id: AC1\n        text: \"go build ./pkg/format/ completes with no errors\"\n      - id: AC2\n        text: \"golangci-lint ./pkg/format/ reports no issues\"\n      - id: AC3\n        text: \"Column alignment exported API is usable from a cmd/ package to produce left- or right-aligned tabular output with configurable column widths\"\n      - id: AC4\n        text: \"ANSI color exported API provides distinct escape sequences for at least: regular file, directory, symbolic link, executable\"\n      - id: AC5\n        text: \"Size formatting output for byte counts that are exact powers of 1024 matches the format specified in the PRD and is consistent with GNU coreutils --human-readable output\"\n```"}]